; A yearless 02/29 read in January 2028 belongs to 2027 (February is
; still ahead), and 2027 has no Feb 29: the date is an error, not a
; silent 2027/02/28, in the journal and in a -b option alike.

02/29 leap day
    Expenses:Food    $1
    Assets:Cash

test print --now 2028/01/15 -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing file "$FILE", line 5:
While parsing transaction:
> 02/29 leap day
Error: Day of month is not valid for year
end test

test reg --now 2028/01/15 -b 02/29 -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing option '-b'
Error: Day of month is not valid for year
end test
